seline_margin": 9.61, "analyst_adjustment": -0.11, "key_factors": ["Klobuchar's lopsided money and name-recognition edge: $7.0M raised vs. $0.4M for Demuth", "Consistent polling lead: every 2026 survey shows Klobuchar ahead, with averages near +9", "Ratings consensus of Likely-to-Solid D across seven outlets and markets pricing her at 92-95%", "Open-seat dynamics, DFL rural erosion, and a $10M pro-Demuth PAC infusion leave room for tightening"], "rationale": "Klobuchar has led every poll this cycle, most by high single digits, and pairs that with a massive fundraising advantage; raters across the spectrum call the open seat Likely-to-Solid Democratic and markets price her near 95%. A single Republican-leaning September poll at +2 hints at tightening, but it sits against an overall polling average near nine points.", "watch": "The Oct. 21 debate and the $10 million outside infusion backing Demuth could narrow the race if late polling drifts toward the most recent Republican-leaning survey.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Open seat: Tim Walz (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Minnesota's governor's race is an open-seat contest between Democrat Amy Klobuchar and Republican Lisa Demuth after Tim Walz chose not to run again. Klobuchar, a three-term senator with high statewide name recognition, has raised roughly $7 million to Demuth's $360,000, though a PAC aligned with Demuth received a $10 million infusion and the contest is already the most expensive governor's race in state history.\n\nPolling since June consistently shows Klobuchar ahead, with September surveys giving her leads of two to ten points and averages clustering near nine. Ratings from seven outlets range from Likely to Solid or Safe Democratic, and prediction markets put her chances above ninety percent. The state's modest Democratic lean and the open-seat dynamic keep this short of a lock, but the weight of evidence points to a Klobuchar win, with the main question being the size of her margin.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9683, "margin": 10.03}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9647, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.931, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9507, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9476, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9456, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9491, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9656, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9546, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9536, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9443, "margin": 8.8}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9456, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9461, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9453, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9445, "margin": 9.5}]}